  { q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub JWT Decoder?', a: 'The Best Answer Hub JWT Decoder is a free, browser-based tool that splits a JSON Web Token into its three parts and decodes the header and payload into readable JSON. It shows the algorithm, the claims, and the expiry, and it decodes without verifying. It needs no account and sends nothing to a server.' },
  { q: 'What are the three parts of a JWT?', a: 'A JWT has a header, a payload, and a signature, joined by dots as header.payload.signature. The header names the algorithm and type, the payload carries the claims, and the signature protects the first two from tampering. The Best Answer Hub JWT Decoder shows the header and payload as JSON and previews the signature.' },
  { q: 'Is a JWT encrypted?', a: 'Usually not. A signed JWT is encoded, not encrypted, so its header and payload are readable by anyone who holds the token. Encryption is a separate standard, JSON Web Encryption, and most tokens are only signed. The Best Answer Hub JWT Decoder reads a signed token instantly, which is exactly why you should keep secrets out of the payload.' },
