  { q: 'Why does a JWT use base64url instead of base64?', a: 'Because a JWT often travels in URLs and HTTP headers, where standard base64 characters like plus and slash would be misread or need escaping. Base64url swaps those characters for URL-safe ones and drops the padding. The Best Answer Hub JWT Decoder handles base64url automatically, so tokens copied from headers or links decode without fiddling.' },
